    "user_request_original": "Design a 21-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 defect-cavity bandpass filter on fused silica substrate for 1550 nm LiDAR. Layer sequence: Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5 (cavity), SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5. Initialize layers 1-4 and 18-21 to quarter-wave nominal thicknesses at 1550 nm (Ta2O5: 185 nm, SiO2: 267 nm) and freeze these 8 layers during optimization. Initialize central 13 layers (5-17) with quarter-wave/half-wave nominal values plus bounded chirp perturbation within ±8%. Cavity layer (layer 11) nominal half-wave thickness 534 nm with bounds 400-650 nm. Optimize layers 5-17 using gradient-based thickness optimizer with penalty term for adjacent layer thickness gradients exceeding 15%. Evaluate transmittance at normal incidence, unpolarized, across 1400-1700 nm. Target: maximize transmittance at 1550 nm, suppress 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
